title: Client-caused 4xx count as node errors in request.finish and the registry snapshot
updated: 2026-10-15T03:10:16Z
---

Noted while building the rerank route (k92), existing behaviour. request.finish is called with ok => 0 for every upstream 4xx, and since k92 for a request refused after admission (400, a document a TEI node cannot take). A failed request counts toward the node's error counter, errors_in_window and last_failure_at in the registry snapshot -- so a client that sends bad requests makes a healthy node look like a failing one to a fronting Skeid. A client abort is already counted apart (k81).

Decide: whether a 4xx that is the client's to fix (400, 404, 413, 422; not 401/403/429, which say something about the node's key or capacity) should be a fourth outcome like `aborted`, counted apart and outside the error window. ADR-worthy: it changes what the registry snapshot's error numbers mean.

2026-10-14 03:57 Empfehlung (nicht umgesetzt, ADR-pflichtig): ja, viertes Outcome neben ok/error/aborted, z.B. 'rejected': 400, 404, 413, 422 (client-verschuldet) zählen getrennt, nicht in error counter, errors_in_window und last_failure_at; 401/403/429 bleiben Node-Fehler (Key/Kapazität). Registry-Snapshot bekommt ein eigenes Feld, bestehende Felder behalten ihre Bedeutung; ADR zur geänderten Semantik, Abstimmung mit fronting-Skeid (Registry-Format ADR 0017, Versionsfeld).

